Aggrieved by the aforementioned actions, the instant petition has been filed by the Petitioner-Union with the following prayers:
"a. Direct the respondent no. 1, DDA to suspend further the demolition (if any) and maintain status quo at the demolished site until all residents are surveyed and rehabilitated as per the DUSIB Policy;
Shakarpur Slum Union vs Dda And Ors on 2 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/131330551/
1 b. Direct the Respondents to not physically dispose/evict the residents from the demolition site;
c. Direct respondent no. 2, DUSIB to conduct a survey of the affected residents and rehabilitate them in accordance with the Delhi JJ slum Rehabilitation and Relocation Policy, 2015;

d. Direct the respondents to put on record the survey of the residents in accordance with the DUSIB policy of 2015;
e. Direct respondents to immediately provide shelter to the Petitioner with proper sanitation, clean water and hygienic conditions;
f. Direct the Respondents to pay 1,00,000/- compensation to the each of the affected family for the loss and suffering due to demolition and inaction on the part of the respondents.
g. Any other order deemed fit and proper in the circumstances of the present case.

